  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLXQT-21" textLabel="CPLXQT-21" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLXQT-21" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="455" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, tissier">The enzyme was shown to form a homo- or heterodimer with itself or the other UGE proteins (UGE1,2,4,5) |CITS:[16644739]|. The enzyme was recombinantly expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;; the purified recombinant enzyme was confirmed to have UDP-glucose 4-epimerase activity |CITS:[16644739]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLXQT-21" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT1G63180-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33194, RXN-9539" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="2" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="98." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="98." />
      <Property key="Species" value="ARA" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16644739" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-7037" textLabel="CPLX-7037" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-7037" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="615" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>This &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; enzyme was isolated through sequence analysis with a variety of genes encoding UDP-D-glucuronate decarboxylases from several species |CITS:[12969423]|. The protein&apos;s function was confirmed by heterologously expressing the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis AXS1&lt;/i&gt; gene encoding the UDP-D-glucuronate decarboxylase in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. Crude extracts of the AtAXS1-expressing &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; cells were incubated with radiolabeled UDP-D-glucuronate and shown to produce both UDP-D-apiose and UDP-D-xylose |CITS:[12969423]|. The enzyme was further purified and demonstrated a requirement for NAD&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt; for activity (NADP&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt; was ineffective). The enzyme was insensitive to EDTA, indicating a lack of requirement for divalent cations for AtAXS1 activity. In constrast with the parsley enzyme, the activity of the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; protein is not stabilized by addition of DTT |CITS:[12969423]|. UDP-D-glucose, UDP-D-galactose and UDP-D-xylose do not serve as substrate. While UDP-D-xylose acts as an inhibitor of AtAXS1 activity, the other two sugar nucleotides do not. Additionally, UDP-D-galactose has a strong inhibitory effect on the enzyme activity |CITS:[12969423]|. While in the case of the parsley enzyme NH&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt; was reported to inhibit the formation of UDP-D-apiose and stimulate UDP-D-xylose synthesis, (NH&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;SO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; was shown to inhibit AtAXS1 activity without affecting the apiose/xylose ratio (similar effects were observed with NH&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Cl, KCl and MgCl&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; |CITS:[12969423]|. The protein was shown to be cryosensitive: storage of the purified enzyme overnight at 0 to 25ºC resulted in 40 to 50% loss of activity, respectively. Storage at -20ºC and -80ºC in the presence of 50% glycerol led to a 50% and 74% decreased in activity over one week, respectively. The enzyme was completely inactivated by freezing in the absence of cryoprotectant |CITS:[12969423]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-7037" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="UDP-D-apiose/UDP-D-xylose synthase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="UDP-D-glucuronate decarboxylase" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT2G27860-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33715, RXN-12444" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="2" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="84." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="84." />
      <Property key="Species" value="ARA" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12969423" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLXQT-17" textLabel="CPLXQT-17" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLXQT-17" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="775" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, tissier">UDP-glucose 4-epimerase catalyses the interconversion of the sugar nucleotides UDP-glucose and UDP-galactose via a UDP-4-keto-hexose intermediate. The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana UGE&lt;/i&gt; gene was shown to complement a &lt;i&gt;Saccharomyces cerevisiae&lt;/i&gt; &amp;Delta;&lt;i&gt;gal10&lt;/i&gt; mutant impaired in their growth on galactose|CITS:[8615692]|. The activity of the enzyme was shown to be dependent on NAD&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt; as a noncovalently bound cofactor. In its reduced NADH form, the cofactor was shown to inhibit that activity of the enzyme. The recombinant enzyme was shown to be only moderately sensitive to high concentration of salts (addition of 400 mM NaCl caused an inhibition of activity of 31% |CITS:[8615692]|). The enzyme was later shown to form a homo- or heterodimer with itself or the other UGE proteins (UGE2-5) |CITS:[16644739]|. The enzyme was recombinantly expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;; the purified recombinant enzyme was confirmed to have UDP-glucose 4-epimerase activity |CITS:[16644739]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLXQT-17" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT1G12780-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-9536" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="2" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="103." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="103." />
      <Property key="Species" value="ARA" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16644739" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_8615692" />
    </Group>
  </Groups>
